From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:30:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 231/342] usb_webcam: MJPEG decoded by the S905's decoder

When meson_vdec and linux-firmware's gxl_mjpeg.bin (meson_vdec_firmware)
can be had, one thread gives each whole picture to the decoder and,
while it decodes that, turns the frame of the one before into B_RGB32
with NEON (i420_neon.c, JPEG's full range BT.601 as libjpeg-turbo):
21 + 12 ms a 1920x1080 frame, overlapped. A picture cut short isn't
given to it, as it would decode the next one into it. The decoder does
one session at a time (a video player's, say), and without it or the
firmware libjpeg-turbo decodes as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
